  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Two parts at their own speeds, converging (docs/plan/prompts/75)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Nancarrow's *Study No. 21*, \"Canon X\", is the piece this exists for: one" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// voice begins slow and accelerates throughout, the other begins fast and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// decelerates, and they cross in the middle. It is the shape the study is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// named after, and there is no way to write it with one clock — a piece with" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// a single tempo can put a *rit.* over everything, and that is a different" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// piece." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// This is polytempo and a gradual tempo change composing, which is the reason" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the two prompts are adjacent: a part's tempo is a fact in the part's scope" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// (prompt 75), and a gradual change is a fact carrying its reach (prompt 73)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Neither knows about the other, and this file needed nothing new from" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// either." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The exports state it as far as each format can. `MusicXML` and MEI attach a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// tempo to a part and a staff respectively, so each part carries its own" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// marking. SMF has one tempo track: every note is written at the frame it" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// actually sounds, so the file plays correctly, and the tempo the file" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// *states* is the piece's. Sonically exact and notationally wrong, said in a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// warning rather than discovered." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Canon X\"" },
    { "kind": "{", "text": "{" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The piece's own tempo: what the conductor's part would say, and what" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the exports state where they can state only one." },
